      "id": "SCF-01",
      "chapter": "lifts",
      "title": "The theta Fourier coefficient selects a Gram fibre",
      "anchor": "lifts-schrodinger-fourier",
      "statement": "For a nonsingular rational Hermitian index β, the Fourier coefficient of the normalized theta mean is the target mean of the sum of the translated Schwartz function over rational tuples of full column rank and Gram matrix β.",
      "hypotheses": "The standard Schrödinger data over E/F include the specified additive and Hecke characters, Weil action, lattice and Haar measures, height, and a test function in the global Fock subspace. Write n for the source rank, m for the target rank. Assume n<m≤2n and n+WittIndex(V)<m. Use the covolume-one Hermitian fundamental region and det β≠0.",
